                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pretty much everything I remember when I played this 20+ years ago. I played on an M4 Mac Book Pro and there was one main bug. Anytime a video was playing and I connected my headphones (bluetooth), the video would freeze and I'd need to reload the game. Not a big deal but it definitely killed the immersion of the moment. Also, I wish they'd added more of the quick jump points for the modern playthrough. They probably just left it as the orignal game though so that's fine. Still good puzzles and a great story. I wish the industry made more games like this. I tried the 3D version of Riven and didn't like it at all (they changed too much) but this original is great if you are feeling nostalgic. On last complaint, and I don't know if this was in the original, I was able to read all the journals except Catherine's. I had to look hers up on a website as the cursive was very, very hard to read. Everywhere else in the game it was fine. Looking forward to Myst 3 and beyond.",
